1. **Files changed:** `src/new_grep/new_grep.c`
2. **Behavior added:** `-h` / `--no-filename` forces the filename prefix off regardless of file count. Combined short-option clusters (e.g. `-Hh`, `-hH`) are supported.
3. **Last-one-wins resolution:** A single `int prefix_mode` (initially `-1`) is updated each time a prefix-related option is seen during the left-to-right argument scan. `-H`/`--with-filename` sets it to `1`; `-h`/`--no-filename` sets it to `0`. Because the scan is sequential and each occurrence overwrites the previous, the final value reflects whichever option appeared last. At output time, `1` means always prefix, `0` means never prefix, and `-1` (unspecified) falls back to the default rule (prefix when ≥ 2 file operands).
